C.push(h2("3.11. Robustness summary"));
C.push(p("Table 6 aggregates the robustness indicators over the full suite: the minimum density and pressure attained during each run, the extrema of transported scalars, and the total safeguard activation counts. The design expectation, supported by the development computations, is a uniform picture: no case requires the safeguard beyond isolated activations at the strongest interactions; the proposed scheme's transported scalars remain exactly within their initial bounds; and its pressure minima are consistently no smaller-typically larger-than the baseline's, which we attribute to the vertex-monotone clamp preventing the locally over-compressive linear states that erode the positivity margin of ψ ≤ 1 schemes when combined with sigmoid candidates. We refrain from claiming a formal positivity guarantee; the observation is empirical and is reported as such."));
